{"id": "EUVD-2026-98712", "enisaUuid": "32efe060-a070-31fc-94d0-9fc717181a42", "description": "FreeRDP from 3.20.1 before 3.32.0 contains an uncontrolled resource allocation vulnerability that allows malicious RDP servers to exhaust client memory via oversized drive redirection read requests. Attackers can send IRP_MJ_READ with Length 0xffffffff, causing roughly 4 GiB of zeroed allocation on 64-bit builds or an under-reserved buffer on 32-bit builds.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T13:27:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:48:39", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-q56j-jjh6-38jf", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.20.1-before-3.32.0-unbounded-allocation-via-drive-process-irp-read"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109947", "GHSA-f7q2-5g46-x57m"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c6889ef9-2264-379e-af4c-0c6bc49dde62", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.20.1 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8e3d01b5-2c33-343c-bcec-5c2d341d2068", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}